# Relativity 37.0 — Omega / Integral Relativity  
## The Invariant Content of All Self-Consistent, Mutually Composable Descriptions

**White paper / academic preprint**

---

## Abstract

Omega / Integral Relativity is the capstone of the relativistic program. It is not another separate theory alongside special relativity, general relativity, quantum reference frames, holography, thermodynamic relativity, complexity-horizon relativity, semantic relativity, or reflexive relativity. It is the integral recognition that all such relativizations are facets of one self-consistent invariant principle. Motion, geometry, frames, locality, spacetime, facts, laws, probability, identity, context, symmetry, topology, vacuum, complexity, boundaries, meaning, and description are not independently relativized phenomena. They are manifestations of a single structural principle:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Reality is the invariant content of all self-consistent, mutually composable descriptions.}
}
\]

Formally, let \(\mathcal{D}\) be the totality of admissible physical descriptions, and let \(\sim\) be the equivalence relation generated by gauge transformations, coordinate changes, dualities, coarse-grainings, categorical equivalences, computational intertranslatability, observer-frame transformations, intervention-context transformations, semantic reinterpretations, and reflexive self-redescriptions. Then physical reality is the quotient,

\[
\mathcal{R}
=
\mathcal{D}/\sim.
\]

The final equation of Omega Relativity is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{The Absolute is the invariant under all admissible transformations, including transformations of the invariant principle itself.}
}
\]

This is not a return to metaphysical absolutism. It is the redefinition of absoluteness as recursive invariance. The Absolute is not a privileged description. It is the fixed point of all admissible redescriptions. Omega Relativity is the omega point of the relativistic program: the closure of relativity under its own universalization.

