## 1. Introduction

Relativity began as a physical insight about motion.

Special relativity showed that inertial frames are not privileged. General relativity showed that coordinates are not privileged. Quantum theory showed that measurement contexts are not privileged. Holography showed that bulk descriptions are not privileged. Quantum reference frames showed that observers are not privileged. Semantic relativity showed that theoretical vocabularies are not privileged. Reflexive relativity showed that even the principle of non-privilege is not privileged.

Omega / Integral Relativity gathers all of these insights into one principle.

It says:

\[
\boxed{
\text{No description is final. Reality is what remains invariant under all admissible descriptions.}
}
\]

This is not a new physical force, a new particle, or a new spacetime geometry. It is a meta-physical and meta-theoretic completion of the relativistic program.

It does not replace physics. It organizes physics.

It tells us what physical objectivity is:

\[
\text{Objectivity is invariance under admissible transformation.}
\]

It tells us what reality is:

\[
\text{Reality is the equivalence class of all mutually composable, self-consistent descriptions.}
\]

It tells us what the Absolute is:

\[
\text{The Absolute is not a description. It is the invariant structure preserved by all descriptions.}
\]

This is Omega Relativity.

