## 6. The Quotient Structure of Reality

Given the totality of descriptions \(\mathcal{D}\) and the equivalence relation \(\sim\), physical reality is the quotient,

\[
\mathcal{R}
=
\mathcal{D}/\sim.
\]

A physical entity is not a description \(D\). It is an equivalence class,

\[
[D]
=
\{D'\in\mathcal{D}\mid D'\sim D\}.
\]

This generalizes familiar physical quotients:

\[
\text{gauge field}
\rightarrow
\text{gauge orbit},
\]

\[
\text{metric}
\rightarrow
\text{diffeomorphism class},
\]

\[
\text{theory}
\rightarrow
\text{duality class},
\]

\[
\text{microstate description}
\rightarrow
\text{universality class},
\]

\[
\text{interpretation}
\rightarrow
\text{empirical equivalence class}.
\]

Omega Relativity says that all physical objectivity has this quotient structure.

