## 14. Omega Relativity and General Relativity

General relativity is another prototype.

A metric \(g_{\mu\nu}\) and its diffeomorphic image \(\phi^*g_{\mu\nu}\) represent the same physical geometry:

\[
(M,g_{\mu\nu})
\sim
(M,\phi^*g_{\mu\nu}).
\]

Physical observables must be diffeomorphism-invariant.

For example, a relational observable may be written as

\[
\phi\big|_{T^\mu(x)=X^\mu}.
\]

The invariant content is not the coordinate representation. It is the relational structure.

Omega Relativity generalizes diffeomorphism invariance to all admissible redescriptions.

