## 23. The Category of All Descriptions

A fully formal Omega Relativity may be expressed categorically.

Let \(\mathbf{Desc}\) be the category of descriptions.

Objects are descriptions \(D\).

Morphisms are translations, reductions, dualities, coarse-grainings, and reinterpretations.

Let \(\mathbf{Inv}\) be the category of invariant empirical structures.

The physical-content functor is

\[
\mathrm{Phys}:
\mathbf{Desc}
\rightarrow
\mathbf{Inv}.
\]

It sends a description to its invariant content:

\[
\mathrm{Phys}(D)
=
[D].
\]

Admissible equivalences are inverted by this functor:

\[
D\sim D'
\quad
\Rightarrow
\quad
\mathrm{Phys}(D)
\cong
\mathrm{Phys}(D').
\]

Omega Relativity is the localization of \(\mathbf{Desc}\) at all admissible equivalences:

\[
\mathbf{Inv}
\simeq
\mathbf{Desc}[\sim^{-1}].
\]

Thus reality is the category of descriptions modulo all admissible equivalence.

