## 24. The Omega Fixed Point

Let \(\mathcal{G}\) be the total groupoid of admissible transformations.

The Omega invariant is the fixed-point structure,

\[
\mathcal{R}_\Omega
=
\mathrm{Fix}(\mathcal{G}).
\]

That is,

\[
\mathcal{R}_\Omega
=
\left\{
X
\mid
gX=X
\ \forall g\in\mathcal{G}
\right\}.
\]

Because \(\mathcal{G}\) includes reflexive transformations of the principle itself, the fixed point satisfies

\[
\mathcal{R}_\Omega
=
\mathcal{G}(\mathcal{R}_\Omega).
\]

This is the mathematical form of the Omega point.

