This is not necessarily a literal measure. It is a symbolic expression of the idea that reality is obtained by integrating over all admissible descriptions and quotienting by equivalence.

In a path-integral-like notation, one may write

\[
Z_\Omega
=
\int_{\mathcal{D}/\sim}
\mathcal{D}[D]\,
e^{i\mathcal{A}[D]/\hbar},
\]

where \(\mathcal{A}[D]\) is an action or consistency functional over descriptions.

This notation is metaphorical unless a precise measure is defined. But it captures the integral spirit of Omega Relativity.

