## 28. Axioms of Omega Relativity

The framework may be organized around fifteen axioms.

### Axiom 1: Descriptions Are Primary Vehicles of Theory

Physics is expressed through descriptions.

### Axiom 2: No Description Is Absolutely Privileged

No description is reality itself.

### Axiom 3: Reality Is Invariant Content

Physical reality is what remains invariant under admissible transformations.

### Axiom 4: Equivalence Is Generated by Redundancy

Gauge, coordinate, duality, coarse-graining, semantic, and reflexive transformations generate equivalence.

### Axiom 5: Self-Consistency Is Required

Only consistent descriptions contribute.

### Axiom 6: Composability Is Required

Descriptions must be mutually composable.

### Axiom 7: Empirical Adequacy Is Required

Descriptions must agree with observation within their domains.

### Axiom 8: Invariants Are Physical

Observables and structures invariant under equivalence are physical.

### Axiom 9: Redundancies Are Not Physical

Gauge-dependent, coordinate-dependent, or interpretation-dependent structures are not physical by themselves.

### Axiom 10: Scale Is Relative

Effective laws may be scale-relative.

### Axiom 11: Meaning Is Relative

Physical terms derive meaning from theoretical and operational roles.

### Axiom 12: Observers Are Internal

Observers are part of the described world.

### Axiom 13: Reflexivity Is Mandatory

The framework must apply to itself.

### Axiom 14: The Absolute Is Recursive Invariance

The Absolute is the fixed point of all admissible transformations.

### Axiom 15: Omega Is Integral

All previous relativities are facets of one invariant principle.

