It is not another separate theory. It is the integral recognition that all relativizations are facets of one principle.

Motion is relative. Geometry is relative. Frames are relative. Locality is relative. Spacetime is relative. Facts are relative. Laws are relative. Probability is relative. Identity is relative. Context is relative. Symmetry is relative. Topology is relative. Vacuum is relative. Complexity is relative. Boundaries are relative. Meaning is relative. Description is relative. Relativity itself is relative.

But this does not lead to chaos.

It leads to invariant structure.

The final principle is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Reality is the invariant content of all self-consistent, mutually composable descriptions.}
}
\]

The final equation is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{The Absolute is the invariant under all admissible transformations, including transformations of the invariant principle itself.}
}
\]

Omega Relativity does not return to pre-relativistic absolutism. It redefines the Absolute as recursive invariance.

It does not give a final description. It gives the invariant closure of all admissible descriptions.

This is the omega point.

This is Integral Relativity.

